    "result_text": "The full build passes with `BUILD SUCCESS` and the acceptance test (`coreFormatAndGlobalSequence`) is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `customerCode` assignment for owners, formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>`, placing each piece of logic in its natural layer:\n\n**Formatting logic** \u2014 new `CustomerCodeGenerator` (`service/CustomerCodeGenerator.java`), a small single-responsibility `@Component`. It uppercases the first three letters of the last name and zero-pads `count + 1` to four digits (`String.format(\"%s-%04d\", ...)`), handling last names shorter than three letters.\n\n**Sequence source** \u2014 added `long count()` to the `OwnerRepository` interface and implemented it in all three profiles (Spring Data JPA via `@Query`, JPA, and JDBC), so the \"current number of owners\" is a cheap `COUNT` rather than loading every owner.\n\n**Orchestration** \u2014 `ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner` now assigns the code only for a brand-new owner that doesn't already have one (`owner.isNew() && owner.getCustomerCode() == null`), so updates never re-stamp it. The count is read just before persisting, and because owners insert eagerly under the IDENTITY strategy, each successive create sees the prior one and the global sequence increments by one.\n\n**Persistence & API surface**:\n- `Owner` model: new `customerCode` field mapped to a `customer_code` column, with getter/setter.\n- `customer_code` column added to all four schema files (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres).\n- `openapi.yml`: added `customerCode` as a `readOnly` property on the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it and MapStruct auto-maps it on read.\n- `OwnerMapper`: ignore `customerCode` when mapping the inbound `OwnerFieldsDto` (it's server-assigned, not client-supplied), matching the existing `id`/`pets` pattern.\n\nNo existing constructor callers of `ClinicServiceImpl` needed updating (only Spring instantiates it), and reused existing count/mapping infrastructure rather than duplicating it.",
